' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Notes. These are the facts a reader of the skeleton cannot recover.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

note top of cron_expression
  The component's one custom column type: it wraps a
  validated string. It carries its own rfl reflector and
  stream operator, and the model declares it
  :is_value_type: true, so the repository entity holds
  the string and the mapper converts through to_string()
  and from_string().
end note

note top of job_definition
  Generated from
  modeling/ores.scheduler.job_definition.org.
  tenant_id is optional because a system job carries SQL
  NULL, which is what nullable_tenant_id selects; the
  domain member is therefore optional too, and the mapper
  maps NULL to an empty optional.
end note

note top of job_instance
  Hand-written, and the one entity in the component with
  no model yet. It is read through the two computed views
  below rather than through the canonical entity verbs.
end note

note right of job_definition_event_traits
  Subjects:
  scheduler.v1.job_definitions_events
  .created / .updated / .deleted
end note

note bottom of job_definition_write
  Everything in this namespace is generated. The deleted
  hand-written scheduler_protocol.hpp declared the same
  traffic under the non-canonical subjects .schedule /
  .unschedule / .schedule-batch, retired in favour of
  put / delete / put_many.
end note

